<main id="content"><h1>Planting autumn bulbs</h1><p>October is the month to get tulips, daffodils and alliums in the ground. Plant bulbs three times as deep as they are tall, pointy end up, in well-drained soil.</p>
<p>Daffodils are the easiest: squirrels leave them alone and they come back year after year. Tulips do best treated as annuals in most gardens, so plant fresh ones each autumn.</p>
<p>A handful of bone meal in each hole helps, and a layer of mulch keeps the soil from heaving in a freeze. Water once after planting, then leave them be until spring.</p>
<p>Happy planting! &mdash; Ruth</p></main>
